# CRPS-01. git's core.autocrlf=true (the Git-for-Windows default) rewrites LF to CRLF in the working
# tree on checkout. Every file under this directory is hashed — the corpus DDL feeds
# schema_fingerprint(), the INR JSON Schemas are read byte-wise by conformance tooling — so a
# platform-dependent line ending would make the same commit produce different hashes on Windows and
# Linux. Keep LF in the working tree too.
#
# The repository-root .gitattributes is unallocated by breakdown plan §4 and must not be touched;
# tools/tests/frozen-paths.test.mjs anchors that rule to the root file, so a sub-directory
# .gitattributes inside this ticket's file-scope is the permitted form.
* text eol=lf
